---
source: crates/kiln-image/tests/overlay.rs
expression: "rendered.join(\"\\n\\n\")"
---
/usr/bin/mytool
  → usr/bin/mytool

/usr/lib/sysctl.d/99-mine.conf
  → usr/lib/sysctl.d/99-mine.conf

/etc/motd
  → etc/motd

/etc/sudoers.d/10-wheel
  → etc/sudoers.d/10-wheel

/usr/etc/sudoers.d/10-wheel
  ✗ /usr/etc is where Kiln puts /etc, not somewhere to write
      write `/etc/sudoers.d/10-wheel` instead

/var/lib/myapp/seed.db
  → usr/share/factory/var/lib/myapp/seed.db
  C /var/lib/myapp/seed.db

/opt/thing/config
  → usr/share/factory/var/opt/thing/config
  C /var/opt/thing/config

/srv/http/index.html
  → usr/share/factory/var/srv/http/index.html
  C /var/srv/http/index.html

/boot/grub/custom.cfg
  ✗ OSTree owns /boot; the bootloader and kernels are placed by Kiln

/home/abdullah/.bashrc
  ✗ home directories are machine state, not image content
      Kiln does not manage login accounts or their files

/root/.ssh/authorized_keys
  ✗ home directories are machine state, not image content
      Kiln does not manage login accounts or their files

/tmp/scratch
  ✗ this is a runtime filesystem; nothing written here would survive a boot

/run/nope
  ✗ this is a runtime filesystem; nothing written here would survive a boot

/proc/nope
  ✗ this is a runtime filesystem; nothing written here would survive a boot

/dev/nope
  ✗ this is a runtime filesystem; nothing written here would survive a boot

/mnt/nope
  ✗ /mnt is not a directory the image has

relative/path
  ✗ a target must be an absolute path

/usr/lib/trailing/
  ✗ a target directory needs a name for the file inside it

/usr/lib/../etc/sneaky
  ✗ a target must be normalized: no `.` or `..` components

/toplevel
  ✗ nothing is written at the top level of the image
